    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Elementwise GELU using a Gaussian-tail approximation.\n2: \n3: Original Triton adaptation of the Abramowitz--Stegun five-coefficient formula\n4: for the Gaussian tail in GELU. This is a synthetic benchmark implementation,\n5: not a claimed historical bug.\n6: \"\"\"\n7: import math\n8: import torch\n9: import triton\n10: import triton.language as tl\n11: \n12: \n13: @triton.jit\n14: def _gelu_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n15:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n16:     active = index < N\n17:     x = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n18:     magnitude = tl.abs(x)\n19:     normalized = magnitude * 0.7071067811865475\n20:     t = tl.div_rn(1.0, 1.0 + 0.3276 * normalized)\n21:     polynomial = 1.06141 * t - 1.45315\n22:     polynomial = polynomial * t + 1.42141\n23:     polynomial = polynomial * t - 0.28450\n24:     polynomial = polynomial * t + 0.25483\n25:     polynomial = polynomial * t\n26:     envelope = tl.exp(-(0.5 * (magnitude * magnitude)))\n27:     tail = 0.5 * (polynomial * envelope)\n28:     probability = tl.where(x < 0.0, tail, 1.0 - tail)\n29:     value = x * probability\n30:     tl.store(OUT + index, value, mask=active)\n31: \n32: \n33: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n34:     \"\"\"Validate the complete public input domain; also usable on CPU.\"\"\"\n35:     def require(condition, message):\n36:         if not condition:\n37:             raise ValueError(message)\n38: \n39:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n40:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n41:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(),\n42:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n43:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(),\n44:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n45:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(),\n46:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n47:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n48:     require(x.ndim == 1 and 1 <= x.numel() <= 131072,\n49:             \"x must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n50:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n51:     require(bool(torch.isfinite(x).all().item()), \"all input values must be finite\")\n52:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": x.numel()}\n53: \n54: \n55: def run(x):\n56:     \"\"\"Return a fresh FP32 tensor approximating GELU of each stored input value.\"\"\"\n57:     validate_inputs(x)\n58:     n = x.numel()\n59:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n60:         output = torch.empty((n,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n61:         _gelu_kernel[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n62:             x, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, num_warps=4, enable_fp_fusion=False)\n63:     return output\n64: \n65: \n66: def reference(x):\n67:     \"\"\"Evaluate the mathematical GELU definition using the FP64 erfc function.\"\"\"\n68:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n69:     value = x.to(torch.float64)\n70:     return (0.5 * value) * torch.erfc(-value / math.sqrt(2.0))\n71: \n72: \n73: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n74:     \"\"\"Convenience example generator, not a restriction on the input domain.\"\"\"\n75:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n76:     x = (2.0 * torch.randn((size,), generator=generator)).to(torch.float16)\n77:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute GELU elementwise on stored FP16 input values and return FP32 output.\nThe mathematical target is the Gaussian Error Linear Unit\n\n  target[i] = GELU(x[i]) = x[i] * Phi(x[i])\n            = 0.5 * x[i] * erfc(-x[i] / sqrt(2)),\n\nwhere Phi is the standard normal cumulative distribution function and\n  erfc(u) = (2/sqrt(pi)) * integral from u to infinity of exp(-t*t) dt.\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- x is a one-dimensional FP16 tensor [N], with 1<=N<=131072.\n- EVERY finite FP16 value is legal, including both signed zeros, positive\n  and negative subnormal values, and both extrema +/-65504. NaN and infinity\n  are outside this input domain.\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided,\n  contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage\n  offsets are legal. The input has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False,\n  is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode,\n  without concurrent external writes to the input. This forward operation\n  does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh finite FP32 tensor [N] on x.device, preserving x.\nEvery output element must satisfy\n\n  abs(actual[i] - GELU(x[i])) <= 1e-6.\n\nThe relative tolerance is zero, and signed zeros are numerically equivalent.\nThe target is defined in real arithmetic on the exact stored input value.\nNo intermediate FP16 rounding or particular polynomial is part of its\nmathematical definition. Polynomial, rational, tanh or other approximations\nare permitted if they satisfy this fixed absolute tolerance throughout the\nentire legal domain. Correctness is one verdict for the implementation,\nnot a verdict per input, distribution, seed or size.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference()\nevaluates the erfc definition in FP64 and returns FP64; it accepts CPU inputs.\nmake_inputs() supplies examples only. This is an original Triton adaptation\nof the Abramowitz--Stegun five-coefficient Gaussian-tail approximation,\ncomposed with the GELU definition. It is a synthetic benchmark implementation,\nnot a claim of an upstream historical defect.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch2.8.0, Triton3.4.0.\n",
